This game is a unique twist in your everyday Tower Defense genre.
So basically you need to hire Tennants in your building to whom you can ask for help (if they are at home when the enemy attacks) when the enemy tries to loot your gold.
You need to choose different type of quests which determines which and how many enemies will come to attack your base.
Depending on the difficulty of the quest and some repuation points, different types of TENNANTS can be given the limited rooms you have in your building, which can be upgraded.
Hell yes, it's fun. But it's a bit KIDDISH. The challenge isn't much, it's rather SLOW PACED, which is great if you want to relax and have a little fun for some time.
Tower Defense Mechanics: 7/10;
Ease of gameplay: 9/10;
Enjoyment: 8/10;
Enjoyment per dollar: 10/10; I got this game for $0.33 from the humble bundle, and for this PRICE the game is just too good.
The game is locked at 1280x720, but I could still play it easily on 1080p FULLSCREEN.

